    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d312">

                <pb facs="1460" n="1398" sameAs="frus:frus1945v01/pg1398"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/6–2045</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chairman of the Soviet Delegation</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gromyko</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chairman of
                        the United States Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Stettinius</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                Francisco</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-06-20">June 20, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: On June 9, in the course of
                    discussion of the American document on trusteeship,<anchor n="75"
                        xml:id="d312-f1"/> I informed Commander Stassen,<anchor n="76"
                        xml:id="d312-f2"/> member of the American Delegation about the desire of my
                    Government to get under its trusteeship some territories in accordance with <pb
                        facs="1461" n="1399" xml:id="pg1399"/> Paragraph 3, Section B of the
                    above-mentioned document. Commander Stassen answered that he had to communicate
                    with the American Government on this matter. On the same day Commander Stassen
                    informed Mr. Novikov, member of the Soviet Delegation that the American
                    Government was ready to support the Soviet Government in the matter of giving it
                    territories under trusteeship. At the same time, you, Mr. Secretary, in our
                    conversation of June 9,<anchor n="77" xml:id="d312-f3"/> also confirmed your
                    consent to satisfy the above-mentioned desire of the Soviet Government.</p>
                <p>In accordance with our agreement the Soviet Government has authorized me to
                    concretize the question on territories under trusteeship for the U.S.S.R. I hope
                    that you will agree to discuss this, question before the end of this
                    Conference.</p>
                <p>Awaiting your kind reply, I remain</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Gromyko</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d312-f1" n="75" xml:id="d312-f1-content">
                <p>Doc. 2, G/26(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>), May 15, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ibid.</hi>, vol. 3, p. 607; for text of working paper for chapter on
                    dependent territories and arrangements for international trusteeship, as of June
                    9, see Doc. 892, II/4/36, June 9, <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, vol. 10,
                    p. 525.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d312-f2" n="76" xml:id="d312-f2-content">
                <p>See memorandum by Mr. O. Benjamin Gerig, June 9, <ref target="#pg1235">p.
                        1235</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d312-f3" n="77" xml:id="d312-f3-content">
                <p>Memorandum of conversation not found in Department files; for Mr. Stettinius’
                    views concerning the Soviet proposal, see his letter of June 23 to Mr. Gromyko,
                        <ref target="#pg1428">p. 1428</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
